  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many servings of peanut butter Toby should add to his toast to reach a total of 500 calories, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of calories in one piece of bread.\n   - A piece of bread has 100 calories.\n\n2. Determine the total number of calories Toby wants to consume.\n   - Toby wants to consume 500 calories.\n\n3. Calculate the number of calories left after accounting for the calories from the bread.\n   - Subtract the calories from the bread from the total calories Toby wants to consume:\n     \\[\n     500 - 100 = 400\n     \\]\n   - So, Toby needs 400 more calories from the peanut butter.\n\n4. Determine how many servings of peanut butter are needed to provide the remaining 400 calories.\n   - Each serving of peanut butter has 200 calories.\n   - To find out how many servings are needed, divide the remaining calories by the calories per serving:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{400}{200} = 2\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, Toby should add 2 servings of peanut butter.\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{2}.",
